{"school":{"dbn":"29Q295","name":"P.S./I.S. 295","boro":"Queens","district":"29","district_label":"District 29","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":566,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"222-14 JAMAICA AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11428","phone":"718-480-2600","website":"https://sites.google.com/schools.nyc.gov/psis295q/home","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/70267","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"PS/IS 295Q provides opportunities for students to Achieve their Educational Excellence, become Responsible and Respectful Citizens; to embrace lifelong Learning in a Safe and Positive Environment through Teamwork within the school community. At PS/IS 295Q, all students are expected to maintain an average of 65% or above in all classes. For our screened middle school program students are on track to take the Regents Exams in Algebra I, Living Environment, Second Language Proficiency and expected to maintain an average of 85% or above. It is a shared responsibility between the school and parents to provide students with appropriate support when they exhibit difficulty in achieving these expectations. PSIS 295Q is a member of the National Junior Honor Society. The objectives of the PSIS 295Q Chapter of the National Junior Honor Society are as follows: create an enthusiasm for superior scholarship; develop citizenship; stimulate a desire to serve; promote leadership; instill in our youth exemplary qualities of character. Middle school students placed in the National Junior Honor Society must maintain an average of 90% in all subject areas to be considered for the highest award. This includes Visual Arts, Music, Foreign Language, Technology, Library, and Physical Education to be considered for the highest award.","start_time":"08:10am","end_time":"02:29pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"Q1, Q27, Q36, Q83, Q88","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Queens Vil